{"dur":170,"ev":[{"t":0.8,"type":"voice","id":"v01"},{"t":5.4,"type":"voice","id":"v02"},{"t":13.4,"type":"voice","id":"v03"},{"t":22.6,"type":"voice","id":"a1"},{"t":34.1,"type":"voice","id":"a2"},{"t":44.1,"type":"voice","id":"a3"},{"t":55.1,"type":"voice","id":"a4"},{"t":70.1,"type":"voice","id":"a5"},{"t":81.1,"type":"voice","id":"a6"},{"t":90.1,"type":"voice","id":"a7"},{"t":100.1,"type":"voice","id":"a8"},{"t":110.6,"type":"voice","id":"a9"},{"t":121.6,"type":"voice","id":"a10"},{"t":133.4,"type":"voice","id":"v04"},{"t":141.8,"type":"voice","id":"v05"},{"t":153,"type":"voice","id":"v06"},{"t":0.8,"type":"sub","d":3.658,"text":"Who is Vishnu? Ask, and you may be given ten answers."},{"t":5.4,"type":"sub","d":7.515,"text":"He is the preserver of the world, the keeper of its balance, often painted blue: the colour of the sky and the sea."},{"t":13.4,"type":"sub","d":7.573,"text":"And whenever that balance fails, he comes down into the world, each time in a new form. These are his avatars."},{"t":22.6,"type":"sub","d":6.491,"text":"First, a fish. In a great flood, Matsya towed the boat of Manu, the first man, to safety."},{"t":34.1,"type":"sub","d":4.676,"text":"A tortoise. Kurma held a mountain on his back, while the ocean was churned."},{"t":44.1,"type":"sub","d":5.903,"text":"A boar. Varaha dived to the bottom of the sea, and lifted the drowned earth on his tusks."},{"t":55.1,"type":"sub","d":10.59,"text":"A man-lion. A demon king could not be killed by man or beast, by day or by night, inside or out. So Narasimha came at dusk, on a doorstep."},{"t":70.1,"type":"sub","d":5.713,"text":"A dwarf. Vamana asked for three steps of land, and covered the universe in two."},{"t":81.1,"type":"sub","d":2.429,"text":"A warrior with an axe: Parashurama."},{"t":90.1,"type":"sub","d":3.63,"text":"A prince with a bow: Rama, hero of the Ramayana."},{"t":100.1,"type":"sub","d":4.071,"text":"A cowherd with a flute: Krishna, who taught the Bhagavad Gita."},{"t":110.6,"type":"sub","d":4.835,"text":"A teacher of peace. In many lists, the Buddha. In some others, Balarama."},{"t":121.6,"type":"sub","d":4.679,"text":"And one still to come: Kalki, on a white horse, at the end of this age."},{"t":133.4,"type":"sub","d":7.094,"text":"Some readers see a pattern in them: from the water, to the shore, to the land; from animal, to human, to sage."},{"t":141.8,"type":"sub","d":8.806,"text":"So who is Vishnu? Perhaps the answer is in the word itself. Avatar means a descent. He is the one who keeps coming down to help."},{"t":153,"type":"sub","d":1.227,"text":"Again, and again."},{"t":0.4,"type":"pencil","d":2},{"t":2.6,"type":"dot","i":0},{"t":2.72,"type":"dot","i":1},{"t":2.84,"type":"dot","i":2},{"t":2.96,"type":"dot","i":3},{"t":3.08,"type":"dot","i":4},{"t":3.2,"type":"dot","i":5},{"t":3.32,"type":"dot","i":6},{"t":3.44,"type":"dot","i":7},{"t":3.56,"type":"dot","i":8},{"t":3.68,"type":"dot","i":9},{"t":5,"type":"brush","d":3,"g":0.4,"pan0":-0.8,"pan1":0.8},{"t":6.6,"type":"brush","d":3,"g":0.4,"pan0":0.8,"pan1":-0.8},{"t":6.6,"type":"sea","d":15},{"t":17.2,"type":"pencil","d":0.9},{"t":21,"type":"dive","d":1.4},{"t":22,"type":"band","k":1},{"t":20.4,"type":"brush","d":1.6,"g":0.35,"pan0":-0.7,"pan1":0.7},{"t":22.4,"type":"brush","d":1.2,"g":0.35,"pan0":-0.3,"pan1":0.3},{"t":22.8,"type":"pencil","d":1},{"t":33.5,"type":"band","k":2},{"t":31.9,"type":"brush","d":1.6,"g":0.35,"pan0":-0.7,"pan1":0.7},{"t":33.9,"type":"brush","d":1.2,"g":0.35,"pan0":-0.3,"pan1":0.3},{"t":34.3,"type":"pencil","d":1},{"t":43.5,"type":"band","k":3},{"t":41.9,"type":"brush","d":1.6,"g":0.35,"pan0":-0.7,"pan1":0.7},{"t":43.9,"type":"brush","d":1.2,"g":0.35,"pan0":-0.3,"pan1":0.3},{"t":44.3,"type":"pencil","d":1},{"t":54.5,"type":"band","k":4},{"t":52.9,"type":"brush","d":1.6,"g":0.35,"pan0":-0.7,"pan1":0.7},{"t":54.9,"type":"brush","d":1.2,"g":0.35,"pan0":-0.3,"pan1":0.3},{"t":55.3,"type":"pencil","d":1},{"t":69.5,"type":"band","k":5},{"t":67.9,"type":"brush","d":1.6,"g":0.35